  "status_text": "You can see all twenty-four switches and still gain nothing over guessing no in this game. Split them into eight triples and use each possible three-switch setting exactly once. Pick a triple and predict whether all three switches there are on. An odd-or-even sum of any switches and pairwise products, with an optional constant, must miss at least 5,040 of the 40,320 arrangements. Always guessing no misses exactly 5,040. Lean checked that limit for every choice of triple (L-lib-632). Proofs are being checked and accepted. Recording and credit resume shortly. Nothing is lost.",
